393 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H2/T(Biodiversity conservation is the core goal of all our actions. For us, conservation is not only a subject, but an approach that permeates all that we do, from our methods to our aimed results. )/E(Biodiversity conservation is the core goal of all our actions. For us, conservation is not only a subject, but an approach that permeates all that we do, from our methods to our aimed results. )/Pg 24 0 R/K[0]>>
endobj

394 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H2/T(OAMa actively contributes to the Technical Advisory Group \(GAT\) of the National Action Plan \(PAN\) for the Conservation of Birds in the Atlantic Forest. In October 2024, Luiza Figueira, Executive Director of OAMa, participated in the first Monitoring Meeting of the PAN\220s second cycle \(2023-2028\). Over the course of three days, around 15 GAT collaborators, including representatives from research institutions, universities and the public and private sectors, assessed the progress of each planned action in the PAN objective matrix. They also discussed the successes and challenges in carrying out each action.)/E(OAMa actively contributes to the Technical Advisory Group \(GAT\) of the National Action Plan \(PAN\) for the Conservation of Birds in the Atlantic Forest. In October 2024, Luiza Figueira, Executive Director of OAMa, participated in the first Monitoring Meeting of the PAN\220s second cycle \(2023-2028\). Over the course of three days, around 15 GAT collaborators, including representatives from research institutions, universities and the public and private sectors, assessed the progress of each planned action in the PAN objective matrix. They also discussed the successes and challenges in carrying out each action.)/Pg 24 0 R/K[1]>>
endobj

395 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H2/T(In December, OAMa published, alongside CEMAVE/ICMBio \(National Center for Research and Conservation of Wild Birds\), the 2024 Socio-Environmental Perception Research Report. The research aimed to identify how society understands and interprets some challenges faced by the conservation of birds and habitats in the Atlantic Forest: loss of habitat, illegal hunting and wildlife trade, introduction of exotic species and release of birds into the wild. In this way, the research seeks to evaluate the effectiveness of PAN Mata Atl\342ntica's communication actions.)/E(In December, OAMa published, alongside CEMAVE/ICMBio \(National Center for Research and Conservation of Wild Birds\), the 2024 Socio-Environmental Perception Research Report. The research aimed to identify how society understands and interprets some challenges faced by the conservation of birds and habitats in the Atlantic Forest: loss of habitat, illegal hunting and wildlife trade, introduction of exotic species and release of birds into the wild. In this way, the research seeks to evaluate the effectiveness of PAN Mata Atl\342ntica's communication actions.)/Pg 24 0 R/K[2]>>
endobj

